# wiki/log.md is append-only: every session adds a block at the end and none edits an old one.
# Two sessions appending at once is the normal case, not a conflict, so git keeps both sides
# instead of writing conflict markers. A union merge can keep both halves of a real conflict,
# which is harmless in an append-only log and wrong anywhere else: do not add another file here.
wiki/log.md merge=union

# wiki/_reminders.md gets a row-aware driver, NOT union. Two writers that each only ADD rows at
# the same spot merge, ours then theirs; any other conflict keeps its markers and stops.
# The driver is per clone (git does not copy it), so register it once; safe_commit.sh does this
# on every run:
#   git config merge.ledger-rows.driver "python3 tools/ledger_merge.py %O %A %B"
# A clone without it falls back to git's normal merge.
wiki/_reminders.md merge=ledger-rows
